<title>USA: ComEd Byron, Ill. nuke near full output.</title>
<headline>ComEd Byron, Ill. nuke near full output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co's 1,105 megawatt Byron nuclear power unit 2 was operating near full capacity Monday, returning from a scheduled outage which began August 8, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's almost at full power,&quot; spokesman Gary Wald said Monday, adding Byron 2 was producing about 1,100 megawatts of electricity as of midday Monday.</p>
<p>The unit resumed electricity production October 4 from the maintenance and refueling outage, Wald said.</p>
<p>Commonwealth Edison is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
